-- title:
--   DVRs from minimal primes of varpi in the finite chart
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a principal ideal domain with fraction field $K_0$, and let $F$ be a field carrying compatible $R$- and $K_0$-algebra structures (so that $K_0 \subseteq F$ extends $R \to F$). Let $j \in F$ be nonzero and transcendental over $R$, and suppose $F$ is finite-dimensional and separable over the intermediate field $K_0(j) =$ `IntermediateField.adjoin K₀ {j}`. Write $A =$ `chartAlgFin R F j` for the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of the elements of $F$ integral over the subalgebra $R[j] =$ `Algebra.adjoin R {j}`, i.e. the integral closure of $R[j]$ in $F$. Let $\varpi \in R$ be a prime element and let $\mathfrak p$ be a minimal prime of the ideal of $A$ generated by the image of $\varpi$. Then there exists a valuation subring $V$ of $F$ such that: $V$ is a discrete valuation ring; every element of $A$ lies in $V$; for $f \in A$, $f \in \mathfrak p$ if and only if $f$, viewed in $F$, lies in `V.nonunits` (the non-units of $V$, i.e. the elements of valuation $<1$); the image of $\varpi$ in $F$ lies in `V.nonunits`; and for every polynomial $P \in R[X]$ not divisible by the constant polynomial $\varpi$, both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ lie in $V$.
--
--   This is the Krull-type statement that the localisation of the normal Noetherian domain $A$ at a height-one prime $\mathfrak p$ above $\varpi$ is a discrete valuation ring of $F$, here packaged as a valuation subring of $F$ whose non-units cut out $\mathfrak p$ and whose restriction to $R[j]$ is trivial away from $\varpi R[X]$, so that $\mathfrak p$ lies over the generic point of the special fibre of the $j$-line. It supplies the valuation-theoretic input for the analysis of the special fibres of the two-chart integral model, and is used by [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_valuationSubring_forall_mem_nonunits_mem_asIdeal_of_mem_toBase`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_valuationSubring_forall_mem_nonunits_mem_asIdeal_of_mem_toBase) and [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.jInvChartInf_not_mem_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.jInvChartInf_not_mem_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span), among others.
